The bug was likely caused by the improper handling of alarm state changes, specifically the enabling and disabling of alarms. The previous implementation relied on the `changeAlarm` method, which was complex and not clearly defined, leading to potential inconsistencies in updating the alarm state in the database and notifying the UI. This could result in alarms not being correctly enabled or disabled, especially after modifications, causing unexpected behavior in the alarm management system.

